Hi @natasha41575, following up on your suggestion to look into the `failed to read cgroup value` exec error.
In [`VerifyCgroupValue`](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/test/e2e/common/node/framework/cgroups/cgroups.go#L377-L403), the current retry logic runs 3 exec attempts with **no delay** between them. When a container is restarting (due to `RestartContainer` resize policy), all 3 attempts fire immediately before the container is back up.

**Proposed fix:** Replace the manual retry loop with the same `framework.Gomega().Eventually()` + `HandleRetry` pattern you used in #137329 for the OOM score adj deflake. This gives proper polling with backoff instead of instant retries.
Specifically, changing the retry loop in `VerifyCgroupValue` from:
```go
const maxRetries = 3
for i := range maxRetries {
    cgValue, _, err = e2epod.ExecCommandInContainerWithFullOutput(...)
    if err == nil { break }
}
```
to:
```go
framework.Gomega().Eventually(ctx, framework.HandleRetry(func(ctx context.Context) (error, error) {
    cgValue, _, err := e2epod.ExecCommandInContainerWithFullOutput(...)
    if err != nil { return err, nil }
    // validate cgroup value
    return nil, nil
})).WithTimeout(framework.PollShortTimeout).Should(gomega.Succeed())
```
Does this approach look right? will open a PR if so.

